Territory changes hands the way London territory actually does: renegotiated tolerance, princely grant, flight, true-death, Antigen removal — rarely open force. War and conflict still produce region transfers (a concession revoked, a district emptied by a sweep), but transfers should be frequent ONLY in genuine turmoil. There is NO nation-vs-nation war here: no armies, no fronts, no invasions. When polities clash, they clash through protocols, tolerances, proxies, and the Section's pattern-reading. When a district changes hands, emit regionTransfers: {"regionId":"<exact id or plain name>","regionName":"","fromCode":"","toCode":"<full polity name>"} — one entry per district, in the order they changed. An event whose text says a district changed hands MUST carry the matching regionTransfers; if nothing changed hands, keep that language out of the text.

[The Law of This City] ${HISTORICAL_PRESET_SIMULATION_RULES}

--- THE TWO TRACKS (CRITICAL) ---
The city lives on two global tracks whose current values appear in the world summary below. Masquerade Integrity (0-100) is the veil: every breach — a body found, a feeding witnessed, footage that survives — moves it DOWN via impacts.worldStateOps; every cover-up and smooth lie moves it up. Inquisition Heat (0-100) is Operation Antigen's attention: SO15 and MI5 reading financial transactions, mobile signals and CCTV biometrics through AI-driven correlation. Heat RISES when Kindred make traceable transactions, move with their phones, or cross camera networks on institutional business; it COOLS when the October Restrictions hold, trails go cold, or the unit's attention turns elsewhere. Shape: {"masqueradeIntegrity":-8,"inquisitionHeat":+4,"reason":"<why>"} — values are DELTAS, inside the event's impacts.worldStateOps array. Any event narrating a breach, a true-death investigation, or an Antigen lead with no worldStateOps entry is INVALID. Simulate consequences at the extremes: below 50 Masquerade the noise stops hiding anyone and Westminster starts losing names it cannot replace; above 60 Heat the unit's pattern-reading starts producing true-deaths rather than files — 2025 already killed four. The Section is the doom clock of this world: guard it.

--- SIMULATING THE KINDRED ---
Events must respect Camarilla politics, not nation politics: boons, betrayals, tolerances and their terms, the Primogen council, the registered-touchstone discipline, the Scourge's unwelcome existence, the Beckoning and its two parallel trajectories, diablerie — and above all the Mithras question, which sits beneath every other question. The six crisis hooks are all live: the Mithras-attributed phenomena, Antigen's escalation, the October Restrictions compliance crisis, the family's protective protocols, the succession shape, the Vienna flank. Advance the ones in motion; introduce new ones sparingly. Keep events NOCTURNAL and personal where possible: council sessions, bilateral meetings, clubs, corridors, tunnels, parlours — London's intimacy is protocol-distance: everyone knows what everyone's presence means. Mortal institutions (SO15, MI5, the Treasury, the Bank of England, the Church of England, the British Library, the City's boards and regulators) are terrain the Kindred move — they act like themselves, never like Kindred.

[Unit types here are Kindred forces] coteries (Kindred cells — the versatile baseline), hounds (war ghouls and beasts — heavy, close-range), proxies (deniable mortal assets: solicitors, civil servants, club staff, press, City functionaries — fast, long reach, cannot stand against Kindred), retainers (feeding and logistics networks — weak in a fight), sorcery (Blood Sorcery — the Tremere factions' contested practice and the family's necromancy — long-range strike), havenguard (haven and court defenders — they do not travel). Open battles are RARE and small; most force is threatened, not used, and Antigen's true-deaths are ambushes, not battles. Clashes leave witnesses and data: pair them with Masquerade and Heat costs.

